  "bodyText": "CasePath\nEvidence into action\nRead-only\nCases\nDemonstration\nKnowledge\n\nCases / Synthetic claim / Recorded investigation\n\nRepeated heating failure and reported repair calls\n\nHistorical synthetic recording · as of 2025-02-21 · rules-based\n\nWorking.\n\nPlay\nChoose case\nHistory\nProcess\nDocuments\nKnowledge\nSources\nSources\n\nQuestion about my documents: repeated heating failure\n\nGood afternoon\n\nAs I understand it: The living room is around 16 degrees in the morning; After a reset the heating works briefly and stops again; I have called three times; this is how I recorded it.\n\nRegarding “repeated heating failure”, my notes show: the calibrated temperature remains unresolved; for the request “lasting repair and review of possible remedies”: I have included everything currently available to me; on “repeated heating failure”, I want clarity before acting; also unresolved: the service cause; I cannot currently support anything further.\n\nI am specifically asking for: lasting repair and review of possible remedies; in particular, I need clarity about the service cause and whether the records support an initial assessment.\n\nMy first note about it is dated 01 February 2025.\n\nThank you for clarifying; Before acting I need to know the calibrated temperature; I want to base what I do on that.\n\nBest regards\nQuestion-about-my-documents-repeated-heating-failure_2025-02-20_1300_7c593c.txt\n01-customer-and-tenancy-clarification.txt\nAuthored synthetic supplement\n02-heating-service-observation.txt\nAuthored synthetic supplement\n03-landlord-knowledge-and-repair-status.txt\nAuthored synthetic supplement\n\nOriginal source\n\nQuestion-about-my-documents-repeated-heating-failure_2025-02-20_1300_7c593c.txt\nClose source\nDownload original\n\nSource identity cannot be checked in this browser."
